  "counting_note": "Do not sum run totals as independent cases: locales repeat contracts; lease61, receipt-batch48 and module-coverage44 overlap base198; repository-wide tests are separate. Base198 preceded final acquisition lease fencing and bounded receipt lookup. Final61 covers changed acquisition/archives and final48 covers projection/isolation/complete stability journeys, all with zero failures/skips.",
  "adjustments": [
    {
      "issue": "Old PG GKG test expected per-document local Event under an unspecified default.",
      "resolution": "Explicit default-discovery and legacy-local-events parameterization now verifies both exact outcomes, retaining all replay/provenance assertions; product default remains AUTO_EVENTS=0."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Read-only diagnostic CLI required coverage through its real module entrypoint, beyond direct main() calls.",
      "resolution": "Actual subprocess checks verify exit2+JSON for a missing database without creating it. Canonical dispatch at the module top avoids duplicate SQLModel registration; no CLI failure is claimed without a reproduced failing invocation."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Acquisition intermediate batch updates must be fenced under the same feed ownership lock as diagnostic publication.",
      "resolution": "Final lease revalidation covers combined feed+batch lock acquisition and stale-owner exits at both manifest and download boundaries. Cursor/diagnostic writes require rechecking the live lease token."
    },
    {
      "issue": "Per-row receipt existence lookups introduced N SQL round trips per prepared chunk.",
      "resolution": "One bounded key-only IN query after offset fencing replaces per-row ORM gets. The final48/locale revalidation includes actual SQL-count checks for both new writes and full rewind/replay, with classified counts and article versions unchanged."
    }
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Actual old PG title B-tree rejects a high-entropy CJK title with SQLSTATE54000; normal application startup removes only the verified obsolete index, then GKG_AUTO_EVENTS=0 updates an already-linked local Event with the complete title.",
    "Repeated startup does not recreate unsafe title/source-domain indexes; constraint/custom/hash/other-schema definitions are preserved or fail safely.",
    "A failed atomic projection chunk retains its cursor and no success receipts; independent source kinds and a later batch in the same kind advance, failed input remains available, and explicit retry/replay does not duplicate versions or receipts.",
    "An actual PG canonical_url B-tree 54000 remains a visible held gap and cannot pin an independent official-event batch; retrying unchanged long input does not truncate or silently consume it.",
    "Global database/lock failures do not create a bad-source feedback write loop; only classified row data faults create durable batch holds.",
    "Old projected/skipped history is explicitly unknown without scanning historical receipts; exact offset progress and measured per-feed window deltas remain available.",
    "Actual intake HTTP status GETs are SQL-only, read-only, and do not scan receipt or article-reading histories or open raw archives/remote services; source probe and projection retry require explicit same-origin POST.",
    "Manifest 404, batch404, TLS, timeout, rate limiting, missing feed, invalid archive and checksum failures retain distinct evidence; probes do not move intake cursors or claim a 200 header response is ZIP verification.",
    "Actual source-tree subprocess probe reports read-only unavailable database as exit2+JSON and does not create it; CLI database connections reject writes.",
    "Inherited NewsNow collection/attention/selection/research handoff contracts pass unchanged in both PostgreSQL locales.",
    "Real Chromium desktop1440/mobile390 exercises source details, explicit probe, retry without offset movement, pause/resume and explicit raw search; default page load does not query archives.",
    "All acquisition diagnostic publications acquire the feed ownership lock together with batch locks; stale lease owners stop before intermediate SQL publication at manifest/download boundaries.",
    "Receipt recognition performs exactly one bounded key-column query per chunk (at most500 keys); skipped rows and complete replay retain transactional offsets, counters and immutable versions without per-row receipt reads."
  ],
