  "limitations": [
    "Controlled synthetic ZIP and HTTP fixtures validate mechanics, not source availability or production throughput; no user host was contacted.",
    "PostgreSQL16.2 was executed; the reported deployment uses17 and was not accessed. Bundled PG lacks pg_trgm, so literal-search fallback was exercised.",
    "canonical_url legacy equality index intentionally remains. Its very long URL failure is isolated and visible; this release does not claim it can index every arbitrary-length URL.",
    "Old historical projected/skipped totals are not rebuilt automatically; operator views use exact batch offsets and explicitly scoped upgrade increments.",
    "Source probe shares the configured receiver30/90-second timeout policy, may wait across several requests, and does not repair upstream missing batches.",
    "Browser source probe is a local deterministic stub; separate transport tests exercise a real local HTTP server with official URL routing controlled by the fixture.",
    "Linux executed; Windows locking/DDL behavior was not executed."
  ],
